["<aside class=\"callout why\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>A surplus SKS (Simonov self loading carbine) was zeroed for a soldier you will never meet. Make it hit where you look before you aim at a deer.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The SKS with its two sights in orange: 1 the rear sight, an open notch on a tangent leaf with a range slide; 2 the front sight, a hooded post.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Two sights, one line</text>\n<polygon points=\"10.0,164.9 10.0,213.2 32.3,205.8 97.4,182.7 121.6,173.1 188.6,171.6 233.2,167.9 292.7,162.6 295.0,158.2 292.7,154.5 195.3,154.5 195.3,155.6 117.9,155.6 114.2,158.2 99.3,160.0\" fill=\"#A8743F\" stroke=\"#6E4A2A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"11.5\" y=\"182.7\" width=\"8.2\" height=\"9.7\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#8C5E33\" stroke=\"#6E4A2A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><polygon points=\"160.7,171.6 160.7,178.3 188.6,179.8 191.5,176.0 190.8,171.6\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"158.1,172.3 160.3,172.3 159.5,179.0 157.7,179.0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M132.8 172.3 L133.9 182.0 L155.8 182.0 L157.3 172.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M146.9 172.3 Q144.7 176.0 146.2 179.8\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"138.3\" y1=\"173.4\" x2=\"143.9\" y2=\"176.4\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"138.3\" cy=\"173.4\" r=\"2.0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"117.1,155.6 117.1,145.5 120.9,143.3 196.0,143.3 196.0,155.6\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><path d=\"M120.1 143.3 L121.6 140.0 Q158.8 138.5 196.0 140.0 L196.0 143.3 Z\" fill=\"#8E9690\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"120.9\" y1=\"147.8\" x2=\"123.8\" y2=\"153.7\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"120.9\" cy=\"147.8\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><line x1=\"184.8\" y1=\"146.3\" x2=\"184.8\" y2=\"149.3\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"184.8\" cy=\"147.8\" r=\"4.0\" fill=\"#C8CCC6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><rect x=\"195.3\" y=\"141.1\" width=\"23.1\" height=\"11.9\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><polygon points=\"197.5,141.1 216.8,137.7 217.6,141.1\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"195.3\" y=\"147.4\" width=\"194.2\" height=\"5.2\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"218.3\" y=\"141.8\" width=\"89.3\" height=\"4.8\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"219.1\" y=\"140.0\" width=\"72.9\" height=\"7.1\" rx=\"1.116\" fill=\"#A8743F\" stroke=\"#6E4A2A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><line x1=\"216.8\" y1=\"145.5\" x2=\"213.9\" y2=\"150.7\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"2.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"216.8\" cy=\"145.5\" r=\"2.5\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"305.7,141.1 320.6,141.1 320.6,153.3 307.6,153.3\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"296.4\" y1=\"157.8\" x2=\"379.0\" y2=\"157.8\" stroke=\"#8E9690\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"379.0\" cy=\"157.8\" r=\"2.0\" fill=\"#8E9690\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><polygon points=\"270.4,154.8 366.4,154.1 366.4,156.3 270.4,155.6\" fill=\"#AEB4AE\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"364.1\" y=\"152.6\" width=\"8.2\" height=\"5.2\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"372.7\" y=\"146.3\" width=\"10.0\" height=\"6.7\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/><rect x=\"376.4\" y=\"138.8\" width=\"2.6\" height=\"7.4\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><path d=\"M374.6 145.5 Q375.5 134.4 377.5 134.4 Q379.5 134.4 380.9 145.5\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><g data-tip=\"Rear sight|Open notch on a tangent leaf. A slide sets the range.\"><line x1=\"209.0\" y1=\"138.5\" x2=\"190.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"209.0\" cy=\"138.5\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#17201A\"/><circle cx=\"190.0\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"190.0\" y=\"75.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text></g><g data-tip=\"Front sight|Hooded post. Screws up or down for zero.\"><line x1=\"377.5\" y1=\"135.1\" x2=\"340.0\" y2=\"70.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"377.5\" cy=\"135.1\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#17201A\"/><circle cx=\"340.0\" cy=\"70.0\" r=\"11\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"340.0\" y=\"75.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text></g><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"230.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"235.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"235.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Rear notch on a leaf</text><circle cx=\"25.0\" cy=\"252.0\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"25.0\" y=\"257.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><text x=\"41.0\" y=\"257.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Front post in a hood</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Rear: an open notch on a leaf. Front: a hooded post <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span>.</li><li>You zero by moving the front post <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the sights in the manual</summary><ul><li>RCMP description: \"hooded adjustable post front sight and tangent notch rear sight\" (99%, Firearms Reference Table).</li><li>\"The front sight is adjustable for zero\" (95%, US Army TC 9-56, 1969).</li><li>Zeroing basics, targets and the 3 shot group method are in <a href=\"#/s/sighting-in/0\">sighting in</a>. Not repeated here.</li><li><button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Zero\">Zero</button>: the distance where the bullet hits your point of aim.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 310\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The rear sight leaf drawn large: marks 1 to 10 for hundreds of metres, from 100 m to 1000 m. The first mark, in orange, is the battle setting for up to 300 m. The slide, in orange, is set by pressing its catch and moving it.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Rear sight leaf</text>\n<polygon points=\"40.0,170.0 360.0,120.0 360.0,170.0\" fill=\"#C8CCC6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"70.0\" y2=\"158.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><line x1=\"97.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"97.0\" y2=\"155.4\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"97.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1</text><line x1=\"124.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"124.0\" y2=\"152.8\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"124.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2</text><line x1=\"151.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"151.0\" y2=\"150.2\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"151.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3</text><line x1=\"178.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"178.0\" y2=\"147.6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"178.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4</text><line x1=\"205.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"205.0\" y2=\"145.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"205.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><line x1=\"232.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"232.0\" y2=\"142.4\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"232.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><line x1=\"259.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"259.0\" y2=\"139.8\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"259.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">7</text><line x1=\"286.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"286.0\" y2=\"137.2\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"286.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><line x1=\"313.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"313.0\" y2=\"134.6\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"313.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><line x1=\"340.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"340.0\" y2=\"132.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"340.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text><line x1=\"70.0\" y1=\"170.0\" x2=\"70.0\" y2=\"152.0\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"56.0\" y=\"214.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"start\">first mark: battle</text><rect x=\"150.0\" y=\"128.0\" width=\"30.0\" height=\"48.0\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"165.0\" y=\"120.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">slide</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"240.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1 = 100 m, 3 = 300 m, 10 = 1000 m.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"262.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Battle setting: for up to 300 m.</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"298.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Press the slide catch, move, let go.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Numbers are hundreds of metres: 1 is 100 m, 10 is 1000 m <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>First mark: the battle setting, for up to 300 m <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: setting the rear sight</summary><ul><li>\"Set the rear sight for the desired range by depressing the slide catch and moving the sight bar along the leaf until the front edge of the bar is aligned with the line below the number that corresponds to the range in hundreds of meters\" (95%, TC 9-56).</li><li>\"The first character on the sight leaf is a battle sight setting that is used in combat, for shooting at ranges up to 300 meters\" <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>For deer at hunting range, set the leaf to the 1 (100 m) mark after you zero, and leave it there (Tip).</li><li>Marks out to 1000 m are military. Your ethical range is far shorter (<a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-07\">chapter 7</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The sight picture: the front post, in orange, centred in the rear notch with its top level with the top of the notch, held on the target.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sight picture</text>\n<rect x=\"60.0\" y=\"70.0\" width=\"280.0\" height=\"150.0\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#FFFFFF\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><polygon points=\"80.0,200.0 170.0,200.0 170.0,150.0 186.0,150.0 186.0,200.0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"214.0,200.0 214.0,150.0 230.0,150.0 230.0,200.0 320.0,200.0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><rect x=\"193.0\" y=\"138.0\" width=\"14.0\" height=\"62.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"110.0\" r=\"26.0\" fill=\"#C9B79C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"200.0\" cy=\"110.0\" r=\"8.0\" fill=\"#B3261E\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"244.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Post centred in the notch.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"264.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Post top level with the notch top.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Post centred in the notch, top level with the notch top <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Focus on the front post, not the deer <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: sight picture details</summary><ul><li>Same rule as any open sight: equal light either side of the post, post top level with the notch shoulders (85%, hunter education).</li><li>Your eye can focus on one distance. Keep the post sharp; the target and rear notch go a little soft <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Hold: put the post top where you want to hit at 100 m (Tip). Practise the same hold every time.</li><li>Low light: an open post disappears early on a dark animal. Legal light still applies (99%, <a href=\"#/s/rb-legal-methods/0\">hunting hours</a>).</li></ul></details>","<p>Point in a safe direction. Finger off the trigger. Unloaded and proved.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"The front sight post, in orange, inside its hood. Turning the post down makes the rifle hit higher; turning it up makes it hit lower. Use the combination tool over the post. Small turns, then shoot again to confirm.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Zero up and down: the front post</text>\n<rect x=\"140.0\" y=\"140.0\" width=\"120.0\" height=\"60.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"190.0\" y=\"70.0\" width=\"20.0\" height=\"72.0\" rx=\"2\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M150 140 Q150 52 200 50 Q250 52 250 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#3A403C\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><path d=\"M162.4 78.3 A40 40 0 0 1 237.6 78.3\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"239.0,82.1 229.3,71.1 239.2,67.4\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"70.0\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Post DOWN</text><text x=\"70.0\" y=\"90.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" text-anchor=\"middle\">= hits HIGHER</text><text x=\"330.0\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Post UP</text><text x=\"330.0\" y=\"90.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"middle\">= hits LOWER</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"232.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Combination tool over the post.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"252.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Small turns. Shoot again to confirm.</text>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"288.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Move the front sight opposite to the miss.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Post screws down: the rifle hits higher <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li><li>Post screws up: it hits lower <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: elevation in the manual</summary><ul><li>\"Slip combination wrench over the front sight post. Turn post clockwise to raise the strike of the bullet; turn counterclockwise to lower the strike of bullet. Remove tool from sight post\" (95%, TC 9-56 training packet).</li><li>Rule for any front sight: move the front sight the opposite way to where you want the hit to go (85%, hunter education). Lower post, higher hits.</li><li>Small turns. Shoot 3 more rounds after each change (Tip).</li><li>The tool is in the butt trap (<a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-05/4\">chapter 5</a>).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Windage on the SKS: the front sight drum, in orange, drifts sideways in its base. Moving the front sight left makes the rifle hit right. It needs a sight tool; a gunsmith job if you have none.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Zero left and right</text>\n<rect x=\"110.0\" y=\"150.0\" width=\"180.0\" height=\"50.0\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#59625C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"170.0\" y=\"110.0\" width=\"60.0\" height=\"40.0\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"194.0\" y=\"70.0\" width=\"12.0\" height=\"42.0\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3A403C\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><line x1=\"160.0\" y1=\"128.0\" x2=\"116.0\" y2=\"128.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><polygon points=\"110.0,128.0 120.8,122.8 120.8,133.2\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"1\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"/><text x=\"70.0\" y=\"70.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sight LEFT</text><text x=\"70.0\" y=\"90.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2E7D4F\" text-anchor=\"middle\">= hits RIGHT</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"232.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The front sight drum drifts sideways.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"252.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Needs a sight tool. A gunsmith job</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"272.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">if you have no tool.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>The front sight drum drifts sideways in its base <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Sight left, hits right. Needs a sight tool <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: windage</summary><ul><li>TC 9-56 says the front sight adjusts for zero but does not describe the windage method (95%, my reading).</li><li>On most SKS the front sight post sits in a drum that drifts sideways; owners use a dedicated SKS and AK front sight tool (70%, owner and armourer guides). Tip: hammering a punch can mar the drum. A gunsmith does it in minutes.</li><li>Same rule: move the front sight opposite to the miss <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Paint pen line across the drum and base after zero, so you see if it moved (Tip).</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A bullet path chart: the dashed line of sight and the orange bullet path, which rises, crosses the line at the 100 m zero, then drops more and more past 200 m. Plan: zero at 100 m (a Tip), practise at 50, 100 and 150 m, and no shot at deer past 150 m.\">\n<rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#EEF1EA\"/>\n<text x=\"200.0\" y=\"26.0\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Zero plan for deer</text>\n<line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"150.0\" x2=\"370.0\" y2=\"150.0\" stroke=\"#1F3D2B\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 4\"/><text x=\"370.0\" y=\"196.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1F3D2B\" text-anchor=\"end\">line of sight</text><line x1=\"40.0\" y1=\"144.0\" x2=\"40.0\" y2=\"156.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"40.0\" y=\"136.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0</text><line x1=\"150.0\" y1=\"144.0\" x2=\"150.0\" y2=\"156.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"150.0\" y=\"136.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100 m</text><line x1=\"260.0\" y1=\"144.0\" x2=\"260.0\" y2=\"156.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"260.0\" y=\"136.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">200 m</text><line x1=\"370.0\" y1=\"144.0\" x2=\"370.0\" y2=\"156.0\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><text x=\"370.0\" y=\"136.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"end\">300 m</text><path d=\"M40 166 Q95 136 150 150 Q230 166 300 205 Q340 228 370 250\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#FF6A13\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><circle cx=\"150.0\" cy=\"150.0\" r=\"6.0\" fill=\"#FF6A13\" stroke=\"#17201A\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"30.0\" y=\"62.0\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Zero at 100 m (Tip).</text><text x=\"30.0\" y=\"84.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"start\">Practise at 50, 100 and 150 m.</text><text x=\"30.0\" y=\"106.0\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#B3261E\" text-anchor=\"start\">Past 150 m: no shot at deer.</text><text x=\"200.0\" y=\"280.0\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#17201A\" text-anchor=\"middle\">The bullet crosses the line at 100 m, then drops.</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Zero at 100 m with your hunting ammunition (Tip).</li><li>Then check at 50 and 150 m. No deer shots past 150 m (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: the plan in steps</summary><ol><li>Clean, dry bore. Gunsmith check done (<a href=\"#/s/mc-sks-01\">chapter 1</a>).</li><li>Rear sight on 1 (100 m) (95% for the setting).</li><li>Rest the rifle. 3 shots at 25 m to get on paper (Tip).</li><li>3 shot groups at 100 m. Move the front post until the group centres on your aim (95% for the method, via <a href=\"#/s/sighting-in/0\">sighting in</a>).</li><li>Same ammunition you will hunt with. Different loads hit in different places <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span>.</li><li>Shoot at 50 and 150 m and write down where it hits (Tip).</li><li>Hornady publishes its 123 grain SST load as +3.5 in high at 100 yd with a 200 yd zero (75%, maker data via a retailer). A 100 m zero keeps it simpler for close cover deer (Tip).</li></ol></details>","<aside class=\"callout rule\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): Chase the group, not the shot.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Zeroing with cheap surplus and hunting with soft points.</li><li>Moving the front sight the same way as the miss.</li><li>Leaving the leaf on the battle mark and wondering why deer shots go high.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\" role=\"note\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Range day: 15 rounds of your deer load. 3 to get on paper, 9 to zero at 100 m, 3 at 150 m. Write it on a card in the butt trap.</p></aside>","<ul><li>US Army, <a href=\"https://archive.org/download/gunmanual_sksmanual/sksmanual.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">TC 9-56 SKS Rifle, Simonov Type 56 (October 1969)</a>: rear sight, battle setting, front sight adjustment, read directly 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">95%</span></li><li>RCMP, <a href=\"https://rcmp.ca/en/firearms/firearms-reference-table\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Firearms Reference Table</a>, sight description, valid 19 October 2026 <span class=\"cert c-hi\" title=\"Certainty\">99%</span></li><li>Hunt Mentor <a href=\"#/s/sighting-in/0\">sighting in</a> lesson (hunter education sight rules) <span class=\"cert c-mid\" title=\"Certainty\">85%</span></li><li>Hornady 7.62x39 123 gr SST data, via <a href=\"https://www.midwestgunworks.com/page/mgwi/prod/80784\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Midwest Gun Works listing</a>, checked 2026-10-23 <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span></li></ul>"]